# Both Dockerfiles COPY their inputs by name -- garmin_coach_loop/, entrypoints/, and the
# two requirements files -- so nothing here is a correctness fix: it only keeps everything
# else (git history, worktrees, tests, docs, this repository's own private/gitignored
# material) out of the build context that gets sent to the Docker daemon before those
# COPYs ever run.
.git
.github
.claude
.agents
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache

# Same private-material categories .gitignore already excludes from source control.
.env
.env.*
*token*
oauth-*
state/
private/
snapshots/
proposals/
approvals/
receipts/
*.fit
local/
application/
mvp/
research/
skill-evals/
sources/
